  "notes": "Casual youth slang from English \"chill\" plus する, meaning to relax and do nothing in particular. Closely related to the slang adjective チルい (chill, laid-back).\n\nREGISTER: Casual slang, mainly used by younger speakers since the 2010s–2020s. Avoid in formal writing or speech.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {家|いえ}でチルする: to chill at home\n- まったりチルする: to chill out lazily",
